Open the page. Both elements use the .highlight class. Are they both red?
&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;
  &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Override a Color in a Stylesheet&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    nav.highlight {
      color: gray;
    }
    .highlight {
      color: red;
    }
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;h1&gt;Override a color in a stylesheet&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;The navigation bar below should be red. Is it?&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;nav class="highlight"&gt;Site Navigation&lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;p class="highlight"&gt;This paragraph uses the same class and should also be red.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
