19.10 Test that the right error message is raised
Run pytest test_raisematch.py -v. Does the test pass? Which ValueError message did parse_count("abc") actually raise — the one the test intended?
import pytest
def parse_count(value):
    if value is None:
        raise ValueError("count cannot be None")
    if not str(value).isdigit():
        raise ValueError("count must be an integer")
    return int(value)
def test_parse_count_rejects_none():
